---
title: "5 · Generate and check the draft"
description: Generate the contract, read it through and, if needed, edit the wording for this client.
sidebar:
  order: 6
  label: "5 · Generate and check the draft"
---

**Who:** the person in charge. **Where:** step 2 **Draft**.

{% steps %}

1. Select **Generate contract**. The contract receives its number when it is first generated (for example SAF-2026-0001), and the PDF opens in the page. A Word copy is saved with it.
2. Read the contract through. The right panel sums up the client, the number, the issuing entity, the template and the totals.

{% /steps %}

{% screenshot id="crm/draft-generated" caption="A generated draft, with download, upload and regenerate." /%}

## Change the wording for this client only

{% steps %}

1. Select **Download Word** and edit the file.
2. Keep the signature marks on the signing page. The upload is checked for them.
3. Select **Upload edited draft**.

{% /steps %}

Do not change prices in Word. Change them on the **Services** tab and generate the contract again.

## Generate again

**Regenerate** builds the draft again from the current services. If an edited draft was uploaded, you are asked to confirm before it is replaced.

{% aside type="caution" title="Edited drafts always need approval" %}
A contract whose draft was edited by hand goes to approval, whatever the discount.
{% /aside %}
